                            <p><p>Amazon is truly a game-changer in the world of e-commerce. Its extensive tools, multiple business models, and outclass software allow sellers, creators, and small and large businesses to conduct sales in convenient ways. While many invest in private label business models, most sellers are attracted to the dropshipping business. </p>
<p> </p>
<h2>What is Amazon's dropshipping business?</h2>
<p>In a competitive marketplace, the dropshipping business model allows you to conduct sales through Amazon without holding and building an inventory. You have to design your storefront, and once the customer orders through the Amazon page, you can direct the order to a third party. The third party or the manufacturer/ supplier is responsible for arranging and shipping the product to the customer. </p>
<p> </p>
<h2>Is dropshipping profitable?</h2>
<p>It is one of the trending models for earning good revenue. The overall success of this business depends on the type of products you offer to customers. The products with the lowest referral fee percentages include appliances, tools, consumer electronics, and automotive products. The overall profit margin through dropshipping on Amazon varies between 10% and 30% (as it incurs referral fees on sales). </p>
<p> </p>
